DATASETS DISTRIBUTED WITH THIS REPOSITORY

The MIT License above covers the source code only. The data files listed below
are derived from third-party academic datasets and are NOT licensed under the
MIT License: they remain subject to the terms of their owners, summarised here.
Details and full references: inference/dati/PROVENIENZA.txt.

1. Derived from NF-UNSW-NB15-v3
     inference/dati/inferenza/unsw_test_raw.csv
     inference/dati/inferenza/unsw_benigni.csv
     inference/dati/benchmark/unsw_bench_50k.csv
     inference/dati/addestramento/unsw_train_raw.csv.7z
     inference/dati/addestramento/unsw_train_contam1_raw.csv.7z
   Source: The University of Queensland, doi: 10.48610/6e0eda1, derived from
   UNSW-NB15 (UNSW Canberra).
   Terms of the authors (verbatim, typos in the original): "The use of the
   datasets for academic research purpuses is granted in perpetuity after
   citing the above papers. For commerical purposes it should be agreed by the
   authours."
   Use is therefore limited to academic research; commercial use requires the
   agreement of the authors. Cite:
     Luay, Majed, Layeghy, Siamak, Mohanad, Sarhan, Sayedehfaezeh,
     Hoseininoorbin, Moustafa, Nour and Portmann, Marius (2025).
     NF-UNSW-NB15-v3. The University of Queensland. (Dataset)
     doi: 10.48610/6e0eda1
     Moustafa, N. and Slay, J. (2015). UNSW-NB15: a comprehensive data set for
     network intrusion detection systems. MilCIS, IEEE.
   and the reference papers listed in inference/dati/PROVENIENZA.txt.

2. Derived from NF-CSE-CIC-IDS2018-v3
     inference/dati/inferenza/cse_test_raw.csv.7z
     (and inference/dati/inferenza/cse_benigni.csv, obtained from it)
   Source: The University of Queensland, doi: 10.48610/ece9b83, derived from
   CSE-CIC-IDS2018 (Communications Security Establishment and Canadian
   Institute for Cybersecurity).
   Terms of the owners (verbatim, excerpt): "You may redistribute, republish,
   and mirror the CSE-CIC-IDS2018 dataset in any form. [...] any use or
   redistribution of the data must include a citation to the CSE-CIC-IDS2018
   dataset and a link to this page in AWS":
     https://registry.opendata.aws/cse-cic-ids2018/
   Cite:
     Iman Sharafaldin, Arash Habibi Lashkari and Ali A. Ghorbani, "Toward
     Generating a New Intrusion Detection Dataset and Intrusion Traffic
     Characterization", 4th International Conference on Information Systems
     Security and Privacy (ICISSP), Portugal, January 2018.
     Luay, Majed, Layeghy, Siamak, Mohanad, Sarhan, Sayedehfaezeh,
     Hoseininoorbin, Moustafa, Nour and Portmann, Marius (2025).
     NF-CSE-CIC-IDS2018-v3. The University of Queensland. (Dataset)
     doi: 10.48610/ece9b83
